  "Id": 2155,
  "Title": "Teaching Dossier ",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "A two hour online session on teaching dossiers was offered by the Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass5634A606CB1B43A687879C8D40F68A45\"><p>\u200bOn Feb 12, 2020, the Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning (QTL_net) offered a&#160;two&#160;hour&#160;online seminar&#160;on Teaching Dossier for AKU faculty members. The seminar was&#160;led&#160;by Dr Jane&#160;Rarieya&#160;(Associate Professor &amp; Associate Director at Aga Khan University)&#160;with the&#160;QTL_net&#160;team.</p><p>The seminar was attended by&#160;20&#160;AKU&#160;faculty&#160;members&#160;from&#160;the following entities&#58; &#160;Institute for Educational Development&#160;-&#160;Pakistan and East Africa, Medical&#160;College&#160;-&#160;Pakistan and East Africa,&#160;and&#160;School of Nursing and Midwifery&#160;-&#160;Pakistan and&#160;East Africa.&#160;</p><p style=\"text-align&#58;justify;\">The&#160;workshop aimed&#160;at&#160;enabling&#160;faculty members&#160;develop&#160;their&#160;teaching philosophy, identify materials for their teaching dossiers which would provide evidence of teaching. The&#160;concepts around teaching dossier, teaching&#160;philosophy, along&#160;with&#160;material evidence as part of the dossier were the highlights&#160;of the session.&#160;Also, the session provided participants an opportunity to reflect on their teaching philosophy and share it in the form of a metaphor. .&#160;</p><p style=\"text-align&#58;justify;\">The participants shared their valuable feedback through&#160;a&#160;Mentimeter&#160;platform, which showed&#160;that they found the&#160;workshop&#160;well organized and helpful. &#160;In particular, they highlighted that the use of concrete examples of teaching philosophy statements and different samples of&#160;teaching&#160;dossier helped them gain clarity on the concept. Overall,&#160;the&#160;seminar was&#160;a&#160;huge&#160;success&#160;as it initiated a discussion around&#160;the need of having&#160;a teaching&#160;dossier and its importance for professional growth at AKU.&#160;Also,&#160;it is a great way to reflect on our goals and outcome&#160;as a faculty and practitioner.&#160;</p><p style=\"text-align&#58;justify;\">The&#160;next seminar&#160;will&#160;be offered in&#160;August 2020.&#160;</p><p style=\"text-align&#58;justify;\">For Inquiries&#58; <a href=\"mailto&#58;Tl_netevents@aku.edu\" target=\"_blank\">Tl_netevents@aku.edu</a>\u200b<br></p></div>",
